# The core: what this framework ships as its working pattern, kept equal to the release.
# One git pathspec a line, comments after a hash sign. A path ending in a slash is a folder.
# A line added or removed widens or narrows the lock (setup.sh), the session check
# (core-check.py) and the deny rules the export writes into
# .claude/settings.json, all together, with no change to any of them.
# Everything else is the user's layer, or a shipped file that is not core (README, examples/).
CLAUDE.md
MANUAL.md
setup.sh
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.claude/settings.json
.claude/core-paths
.claude/hooks/
.claude/agents/
.claude/skills/
